WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.004
Chinese leader Xi Jinping flies

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:04.671
to Moscow

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.638
to meet with Russian

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.240
President Vladimir Putin,

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.375
his first visit

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.111
since Russia invaded Ukraine.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:13.380
It's a powerful show of Xi's emboldened

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.647
diplomatic ambitions

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:17.817
and Beijing support for Moscow

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.352
to jump in today.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:19.953
Chinese foreign

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:20.687
ministry said

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.788
the country's, quote

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:24.391
proposition boils down to one sentence,

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.060
which is to urge peace and promote talks.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.996
Beijing has tried to present itself

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:32.132
as a neutral peace broker on Ukraine.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.401
Publishing a position paper last month

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.804
calling for a political settlement

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.373
and casting Xi as a global statesman

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:41.941
with fresh momentum

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:42.976
after helping Saudi

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.377
Arabia and Iran

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.112
broker a historic deal

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.481
to restore diplomatic ties.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.550
But Western leaders are skeptical

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.819
of Beijing's portrayal as a mediator.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.487
He and Putin declared

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.689
a no limits partnership last year

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.857
when Putin visited

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.392
Beijing for the Winter Olympic

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.827
opening ceremony.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:01.995
This is a year

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:05.165
she has met Putin in person 39 times

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.200
since becoming China's leader,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.203
even exchanging gifts, including pandas.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.939
China has refused

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.174
to condemn the invasion

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:16.042
or even call it an invasion.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.710
Instead, Beijing has parroted

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.279
the Kremlin's misinformation

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.282
while blaming Naito on China's heavily

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.716
censored social media.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.985
It's all hearts and thumbs up emojis.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:26.686
In response

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.221
to the government's official post

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.722
about the state visit

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.291
with comments like Hope

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.826
Russia will win soon.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:33.960
Hope there will be world

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.727
peace

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.030
and long live China-Russia friendship.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.799
Beijing has also strengthened

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:42.135
economic and military ties with Moscow

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.069
by boosting

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.471
trade and holding frequent

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.773
military exercises.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.308
While Western officials

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.375
have raised concerns

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.111
that China may be considering

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.145
providing Russia

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.147
with lethal military aid.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.149
Beijing has denied the accusation.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.251
Last month, Putin told

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:59.385
China's top diplomat

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.553
Wang Yi and Moscow

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.287
that relations

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.522
between their countries

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:05.291
are reaching new milestones.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.426
The two nations,

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.327
bound together

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.329
by their shared vision for a new world

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:09.863
order,

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:12.665
no longer dominated by the West and Sea.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.434
And while she has spoken

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.702
to Putin multiple times

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.936
since the invasion,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.271
virtually and in-person

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.472
and he's not yet

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.940
had a single phone call

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.142
with Ukrainian President

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.077
Volodymyr Zelensky,

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.912
though Ukraine's presidential advisor

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.147
says negotiations

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.681
about a potential Zelensky

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.717
Xi conversation are ongoing

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.486
as she heads to Russia.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.088
The ability of China to help

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.924
resolve the conflict hangs in the balance

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.727
Selina Wang, CNN, Beijing.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.362
I want to turn now to China.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:42.795
This week,

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.563
Chinese President

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.531
Xi Jinping

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.965
will meet with Russian President

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.001
Vladimir Putin in Moscow.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:48.334
Of course,

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.669
these two leaders will discuss

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.571
Ukraine as China continues

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:53.139
to try to portray itself

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.807
as a neutral party

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.210
that could be an honest peace broker.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.411
Now, you sit on the House

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.046
Committee on China.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.347
What strategy

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.448
do you think she is trying

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.484
to implement here?

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.788
For the last 70 years,

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.657
the triangle between China, Russia

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:12.158
and the United States has been

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.560
the most important set

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.395
of international relationships

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.062
in the world.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.430
And clearly, right now, Xie

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.866
Jingping is settling up to Russia

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.100
as it prepares to compete

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.335
with the United States

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.337
in the 21st century.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.173
If Xie Jingping decides to send weapons

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:27.874
to Russia

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.442
for its brutal, unprovoked

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.010
invasion of Ukraine,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.444
that would be

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.879
the most significant development

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.380
in that war since the invasion itself.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.648
On February 24th.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.951
And the United States and its allies

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:38.851
need to be prepared

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.786
to respond

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.888
with severe sanctions

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.823
and international condemnation.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:46.125
Whether those arms sales happen overtly

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.460
or covertly

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.095
because China does have a long track

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:51.264
record of covert arms shipments

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.066
over the last 30 years.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.400
But it really just reminds us

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.502
that we can't rely on the goodwill

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.871
or the good judgment and see Jingping

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:01.674
he is bent on a world order

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.375
in which China is at

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:03.810
the top of a hierarchy.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.178
It's in direct competition

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.347
to the rules based international order

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.616
where right might does not make right

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:10.883
that the United States helped

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.552
put together after World War Two.

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.920
And we've got to defend it forcefully.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.322
On the world stage. Economic alliances,

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:21.527
initiatives to strengthen democracy,

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.896
diplomacy and security initiatives

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.231
We need to do all of this

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:25.732
with countries

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:26.532
like Nigeria,

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.534
India, Brazil, Mexico,

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.336
the rising nations of the global South

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.305
to build a web of alliances

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:34.641
against the Chinese Communist Party.

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:35.308
On the topic,

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.542
you were recently part of a U.S.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.611
delegation that traveled to Taiwan.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:40.880
So what are the geopolitical implications

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:41.981
of XI and China

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:42.882
potentially trying

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.451
to get more involved in the Ukraine war?

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.855
Taiwan crystallizes the threat

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.790
from the Chinese Communist Party

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.292
and the United States.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.593
One needs to continue

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.295
to send arms to Taiwan

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.129
as it prepares

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.297
its strategy

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.531
of defense in-depth

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.566
against a potential Chinese invasion.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.302
We should also work with Taiwan

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:03.636
on their energy security.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.070
Right now,

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.204
they have two to three weeks

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:06.372
of energy reserves.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:06.906
That's

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.041
not a good situation to be in

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.075
when you're an island faced

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.810
with an amphibious

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.112
invasion or a blockade for that matter.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:13.813
And finally,

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:15.615
and this really applies to Taiwan,

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.216
but everywhere else in the world,

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.118
especially in democracies,

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.553
we have got to do a better job

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.954
of countering disinformation

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:22.655
and propaganda.

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.956
We should be supporting

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.491
local journalism efforts.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.192
We should be holding

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:27.226
the social media companies

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.895
to account for how they allow

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:30.296
disinformation and deepfakes

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:33.099
to propagate, because the Chinese are

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.967
launching concerted propaganda

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.769
efforts throughout the world.

